    <id>https://www.nber.org/papers/w35472</id>
    <title>Estimating the Economic Effects of Federally Funded R&amp;D</title>
    <updated>2026-07-01T00:00:00+00:00</updated>
    <author>
      <name>Sheila Campbell, Jaeger Nelson, Eli A. Schrag, Heidi L. Williams &amp; Caleb K. Wroblewski</name>
    </author>
    <content>&lt;b&gt; NBER Working Papers&lt;/b&gt; &lt;br&gt;In recent years, there has been Congressional interest in changing various policies related to research and development (R&amp;D). Recent legislation has included provisions that would modify federal funding for R&amp;D investments and tax provisions affecting the after-tax price of R&amp;D. The Congressional Budget Office (CBO) has developed analytical frameworks for estimating how changes in R&amp;D investments affect the economy and the federal budget. This paper describes the agency’s current analytical framework for modeling the economic effects of changes in federal funding for R&amp;D, focusing on two distinct approaches that CBO has developed: an R&amp;D capital stock approach and an R&amp;D components approach.</content>
